    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0188" n="1022" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1022"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/7602</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-21T16:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 21, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 21, 11.10
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9154. War Trade Board [from Frothingham]:</p>
                <p>No. 318. Fuller. Your 139. May we understand coordination proposals through
                    British Embassy per our 183 have received final approval, and that at time
                    review of cases Washington, London, Paris, respectively, agreed upon, additions
                    or removals will be made, simultaneously to respective official lists?
                    Frothingham.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
